    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nTo multiply fractions, we multiply the numerators, multiply the denominators, and simplify (if necessary).\n\nContent:\nFor example, to multiply [MATH: \\dfrac 1 {2} \\times \\dfrac 1 {3},] we multiply the numerators and we multiply the denominators:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}2} \\times \\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\color{red}3} = \\dfrac {{\\color{blue}1}\\times {\\color{blue}1}} {{\\color{red}2}\\times {\\color{red}3}} = \\dfrac{1}{6}]\n\nContent:\nNotice that we get the same answer when we use a fraction model.\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/361e9716adad9331e25e7b2b7c32bf2e]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Multiplying Fractions by Unit Fractions\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\dfrac 3 {7} \\times \\dfrac 1 {4}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 3 {7} \\times \\dfrac 1 {4} = \\dfrac {3\\times 1} {7\\times 4} = \\dfrac{3}{28}]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (1)/(4) \u00d7 (1)/(5) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (1)/(45)]\nb. [MATH: (1)/(9)]\nc. [MATH: (4)/(5)]\nd. [MATH: (1)/(20)]\ne. [MATH: (2)/(5)]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (4)/(7) \u00d7 (1)/(9) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (2)/(9)]\nb. [MATH: (4)/(21)]\nc. [MATH: (4)/(63)]\nd. [MATH: (5)/(16)]\ne. [MATH: (2)/(31)]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Multiplying Fractions\n\nExample Prompt:\nMultiply [MATH: \\dfrac 2 {9} \\times \\dfrac 4 {5}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 2 {9} \\times \\dfrac 4 {5} = \\dfrac {2\\times 4} {9\\times 5} = \\dfrac{8}{45}]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (4)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(7) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (5)/(12)]\nb. [MATH: (15)/(28)]\nc. [MATH: (7)/(12)]\nd. [MATH: (7)/(35)]\ne. [MATH: (12)/(35)]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (7)/(2) \u00d7 (9)/(4) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (8)/(3)]\nb. [MATH: (24)/(9)]\nc. [MATH: (17)/(6)]\nd. [MATH: (54)/(7)]\ne. [MATH: (63)/(8)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Multiplying Fractions When Simplification is Needed\n\nExample Prompt:\nMultiply [MATH: \\dfrac 5 {6} \\times \\dfrac 3 {4}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac 5 {6} \\times \\dfrac 3 {4} = \\dfrac {5\\times 3} {6\\times 4} = \\dfrac{15}{24}]\n\nWe reduce this fraction to its simplest form by dividing the numerator and denominator by [MATH: 3\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac {15} {24} = \\dfrac {15\\div 3} {24\\div 3} = \\dfrac{5}{8}]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (1)/(2) \u00d7 (4)/(5) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (6)/(7)]\nb. [MATH: (1)/(5)]\nc. [MATH: (2)/(5)]\nd. [MATH: (5)/(6)]\ne. [MATH: (3)/(8)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (1)/(3) \u00d7 (6)/(7) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (2)/(3)]\nb. [MATH: (1)/(3)]\nc. [MATH: (3)/(7)]\nd. [MATH: (7)/(3)]\ne. [MATH: (2)/(7)]"
